<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Daudpota</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Daudpotra</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Daudpota, or Daudpotra, are a tribe from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a> whose chiefs claim descent from the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a> and therefore use the family name Abbasi. In the early 18th century a branch moved from upper Sindh to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutlej-river">Sutlej</a> valley, where its leaders founded Bahawalpur and ruled the princely state of Bahawalpur as nawabs until it merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-pakistan">West Pakistan</a> in 1955.</p></div>
